PTX 2+2W+alias+observers
"P0 writes x and then its alias y; P1 writes y and then x; P2 reads y twice and P3 reads x twice, all relaxed at .cta. Accesses through different virtual addresses behave as if in different proxies (8.6), so program order does not order each writer's two writes, and the observers may see 2 before 3 and 4 before 1: allowed."
{
x=0 @cta 0;
y @ generic aliases x;
P2:r0=0;
P2:r1=0;
P3:r0=0;
P3:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,gpu 0         | P1@cta 0,gpu 0         | P2@cta 0,gpu 0          | P3@cta 0,gpu 0          ;
 st.relaxed.cta x, 1    | st.relaxed.cta y, 3    | ld.relaxed.cta r0, y    | ld.relaxed.cta r0, x    ;
 st.relaxed.cta y, 2    | st.relaxed.cta x, 4    | ld.relaxed.cta r1, y    | ld.relaxed.cta r1, x    ;
exists
(P2:r0 == 2 /\ P2:r1 == 3 /\ P3:r0 == 4 /\ P3:r1 == 1)
